    "Just to confirm the inventory flow: for each month, end-of-month inventory = start-of-month inventory + purchases that month − sales that month, and the sales in that month cannot exceed the start-of-month inventory plus that month's purchases (i.e., you can sell units you just bought in the same month). Is that correct?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for confirmation of a single, unified inventory flow rule (the equation and the associated sales constraint), which constitutes one semantically independent clarification question."
